{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable","id":1505579,"title":"(V5) Is a low generation campaign sustainable?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-17T12:53:11-07:00","id":1505579,"title":"(V5) Is a low generation campaign sustainable?","content":"Hello there,<br /> <br /> I am planning a historical campaign using Dark Ages V20, which I adore, but I had planned on storytelling using V5 for my group sometime and with the players guide on the horizon access to all 13 clans is much more affordable.<br /> <br /> So I pondered how sustainable low Generation PCs are with the V5 rules as written? High Blood Potency seems to have a really harsh effect on hunger and feeding, which I find rather interesting to explore, but I wonder if it would be frustrating in play...I guess frustration is rather subjectic but I hope you get my gist.<br /> <br /> So does anybody here have some experience with low gen PCs or can comment on low generation / high BP in play? Let's say starting Generation would be 7 or 8 but not lower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T14:31:06-07:00","id":1505591,"title":"","content":"You'd have to homebrew Humanity if you want to run a game about high blood potency characters, because they are going to have to eat people routinely. By rights, high blood potency characters should either all be wights, or all have been killed due to constant frenzies and beastial failures/messy criticals.<br /> <br /> Since they don't allow Paths anymore, Humanity must somehow be sustainable for creatures who eat people on a weekly basis. Somehow. Really, this system breaks down at high blood potency, because high blood potency characters are intended to be NPCs whose ability to maintain a four Humanity and not suffer constant beastial failures and messy criticals is handwaved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T15:09:54-07:00","id":1505598,"title":"","content":"Not as a player character as the higher the blood potency is for a kindred, the higher the drawbacks and clan banes are any given person and even playing one with a blood potency of four or five comes with a cost to humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T15:43:38-07:00","id":1505605,"title":"","content":"It's unplayable. Hunger dice/feeding restrictions will destroy you. Also there are no fun roads. I can't fathom wanting to play v5 when you have knowledge of other editions, but dark ages is even more extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T23:05:39-07:00","id":1505638,"title":"","content":"Hello again,<br /> <br /> thank you four all your impressions! I was going to stick do DA V20 anyway since the setting book I use was written with it in mind, but I wondered about it after reading V5 core recently.<br /> <br /> I guess I postpone V5 until after my current campaign plans are done.<br /> <br /> Cheers!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T01:12:34-07:00","id":1505648,"title":"","content":"I'd go &quot;yes but youre probably going to have to home brew&quot;, its not v5 that its bad or da20 is better its just youre not playing to the games strengths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T10:30:32-07:00","id":1505688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacedigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable#post1505579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello there,<br /> <br /> I am planning a historical campaign using Dark Ages V20, which I adore, but I had planned on storytelling using V5 for my group sometime and with the players guide on the horizon access to all 13 clans is much more affordable.<br /> <br /> So I pondered how sustainable low Generation PCs are with the V5 rules as written? High Blood Potency seems to have a really harsh effect on hunger and feeding, which I find rather interesting to explore, but I wonder if it would be frustrating in play...I guess frustration is rather subjectic but I hope you get my gist.<br /> <br /> So does anybody here have some experience with low gen PCs or can comment on low generation / high BP in play? Let's say starting Generation would be 7 or 8 but not lower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot to ask is your player characters going to be neonates or ancilla's? In that case you could play lower generation characters at there base blood potency such as 3 dots for a member of the 7th generation. I would keep elders and the ancients off the table for player characters inmho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T12:22:48-07:00","id":1505695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable?p=1505648#post1505648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go &quot;yes but youre probably going to have to home brew&quot;, its not v5 that its bad or da20 is better its just youre not playing to the games strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I would have had to homebrew anyway if I would use V5 since it has no Baali whom feature heavily in the planned campaign.<br /> <br /> Storytellers Vault is truly a blessing in that regard I must say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25379,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","user":"Spacedigger","date":". 03-18-2023, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-18T12:30:14-07:00","id":1505696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable?p=1505688#post1505688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I forgot to ask is your player characters going to be neonates or ancilla's? In that case you could play lower generation characters at there base blood potency such as 3 dots for a member of the 7th generation. I would keep elders and the ancients off the table for player characters inmho.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a campaign in Ancient Mesopotamia based on the imho wonderful Storytellers Vault supplement &quot;Vampire Age of the Living Gods&quot;. My players will be Neonates of 7th Generation. In V5 that would be BP 3 as you pointed out so no feeding on animals. Time will go by very slowly so natural BP Increase is not very likely for a time.<br /> <br /> As I said I will run the Campaign with DA V20 rules because the supplement was written with it in mind and is easiest to run as written.<br /> <br /> I might come back to V5 when we play something closer to modern day, maybe Victorian or something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thank you for the advice nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T10:32:53-07:00","id":1505791,"title":"","content":"I brought it up as you could swap out the 10/11th generation for the 8/9th generation for the ancilla status and use the rules for that. But it will be a lot of homebrewing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T14:17:57-07:00","id":1505818,"title":"","content":"Step One: Run Revised or V20 because it's actually mostly coherent. <br /> Step Two: Replace Generation with Blood Potency, which is equal to your lowest of your Clan Disciplines, starting at 0 = 13th Gen. Past Blood Potency 5 you need to eat someone of equal or greater Blood Potency to get more powerful. <br /> Step Three: Throw out your V5 books because it makes heresy into canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-19T17:32:42-07:00","id":1505851,"title":"","content":"I will disagree. It's entirely sustainable in 5e. Humanity is cool because the storyteller and players can work together to adjust chronicle tents and personal tenets as the campaign continues. This makes it easy to have your campaign shift over the decades and centuries.<br /> <br /> There's enough simple knobs to twist to make V5 a breeze. There will need to be a few adjustments for clan weaknesses etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T07:22:31-07:00","id":1506043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable?p=1505791#post1505791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I brought it up as you could swap out the 10/11th generation for the 8/9th generation for the ancilla status and use the rules for that. But it will be a lot of homebrewing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for taking so long to respond.<br /> <br /> I see what you mean. I would have just used the Neonate Character Creation but with 7/8 th Gen characters.<br /> <br /> My main concern was directed to the side effects of BP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T07:28:14-07:00","id":1506044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RadioFreeDeath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable?p=1505851#post1505851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will disagree. It's entirely sustainable in 5e. Humanity is cool because the storyteller and players can work together to adjust chronicle tents and personal tenets as the campaign continues. This makes it easy to have your campaign shift over the decades and centuries.<br /> <br /> There's enough simple knobs to twist to make V5 a breeze. There will need to be a few adjustments for clan weaknesses etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, Chronicle Tenents are rather flexible in V5 which is to my liking. Finding the exact <b>three </b>to evoke the moods of your chronicle is not always easy imo, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T16:08:49-07:00","id":1506076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacedigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable?p=1506043#post1506043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry for taking so long to respond.<br /> <br /> I see what you mean. I would have just used the Neonate Character Creation but with 7/8 th Gen characters.<br /> <br /> My main concern was directed to the side effects of BP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are ways around the side effects of BP. Some powers allow it (Animal Succulence), drinking from another Kindred (and you don't have to drink from the vein, they can cut themselves and drain it into a cup), drinking from other supernatural creatures, not using powers willy-nilly to raise your Hunger. Elders also have ways to mitigate the Hunger increases with things like the Discipline rouse check rerolls that come with high BP. It's sustainable, you just... well, have to play like Elders play: smart and thoughtful and with the Eternal Struggle in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T22:16:27-07:00","id":1520081,"title":"","content":"To V5, it would demand so much home brew that you could brew your own system. I STILL don't understand how the SI didn't get every vampire with all the bestial and messy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T23:36:32-07:00","id":1520083,"title":"","content":"I think it's one of those inconsistencies that happen between lore and system, it's like those video games that in history the PC doesn't like to kill, but in gameplay it does it frequently and we just overlook it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T00:04:20-07:00","id":1520084,"title":"","content":"I have homebrewed a more sustainable for lower generation feeding restrictions chart, if anyone is interested","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T09:40:52-07:00","id":1520120,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in your idea Microcuchon on how your worked out the feeding problems for Kindred of lower generations as we have currently two 9th generation npc's and one 8th generation one in our game and I'm been thinking of possibly fleshing out my character's 4th generation grandsire 5 steps removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T15:00:37-07:00","id":1520151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacedigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable?p=1506044#post1506044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, Chronicle Tenents are rather flexible in V5 which is to my liking. Finding the exact <b>three </b>to evoke the moods of your chronicle is not always easy imo, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. The thing about chronicle tenets, is they can easily be manipulated to reflect cultural norms of the period.<br /> <br /> The humanist ideals which inform a contemporary understanding of human rights, life, and dignity -- and consequently, inform modern nights chronicle tenets -- were by and large a product of the Renaissance and Enlightenment. Just one example I can name offhand, punishment for tax evasion was often more severe than for murder...well, unless you couldn't afford weregild, in which case you were evading taxes. And, that's real history, but we're talking about the Dark Medieval which is going to be <i>so much worse</i>.<br /> <br /> A chronicle tenet which flatly prohibits murder, just isn't going to cut it for a v5-based Dark Ages game. Low-generation vampires, particularly those of high clans, can and should be able to get their cherry Capri Sun on without obtaining Stains, because most people aren't going to be considered &quot;people&quot; to begin with. People are certainly free to take exception to this -- as they should -- but normalized monstrosity is part of the personal horror of <i>this particular</i> setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T06:48:42-07:00","id":1520192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable?p=1520120#post1520120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in your idea Microcuchon on how your worked out the feeding problems for Kindred of lower generations as we have currently two 9th generation npc's and one 8th generation one in our game and I'm been thinking of possibly fleshing out my character's 4th generation grandsire 5 steps removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The chart uses a combination of Generation, age, Humanity and previous experiences with Vitae. We decided to build it when we moved our V20 ongoing campaign to V5, but the 8th and 9th generation characters became unplayable. We also made an attempt to link to the lore we had previously established, with characters such as Lucian or Critias who didn't suffer from Methuselah's Thirst","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T14:10:16-07:00","id":1520236,"title":"","content":"Did they ever say why certain ancients didn't suffer the Methuselah Thirst flaw in the game at all Microuchon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T18:10:59-07:00","id":1520249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable?p=1505818#post1505818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Step One: Run Revised or V20 because it's actually mostly coherent.<br /> Step Two: Replace Generation with Blood Potency, which is equal to your lowest of your Clan Disciplines, starting at 0 = 13th Gen. Past Blood Potency 5 you need to eat someone of equal or greater Blood Potency to get more powerful.<br /> Step Three: Throw out your V5 books because it makes heresy into canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never cared for Revised. I prefer 1st with 2nd edition rule book. I used DAV20 and V20 and both are pretty comprehensive, but nothing beats the original VTM for tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T23:31:03-07:00","id":1520264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1505579-v5-is-a-low-generation-campaign-sustainable?p=1520236#post1520236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did they ever say why certain ancients didn't suffer the Methuselah Thirst flaw in the game at all Microuchon?</div> </div> </div> </div>A clear rule it's never given, but I am under the impression that Humanity and Diablerie have a big role and it's something I have baked into my homebrew. As a example, in CbN1 you have two Methuselah's of the same age and Generation, but only the one that has a low humanity rate and has arrived to her Generation through Diablerie suffers from the Thirst. It's a shame they forgot all of that when they created V5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T10:00:27-07:00","id":1520309,"title":"","content":"Thanks Microcuchon as I was stuck on having what kind of feeding problems my homebrewed 4th generation Malkavian might have as he was born 1004 BCE and embraced around 967 BCE and I didn't want to give him the thirst flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}